# MUTABLE TERRAIN (M17 phase 8). A fixture.
#
# A three-cell isthmus across a hole, and it is the ONLY way from the entry rows
# to the exit rows: a crumble in the middle lane, a timed block either side of it.
# Everything else on row 4 is a gap.
#
# That shape is deliberate. The flood must route THROUGH a temporary cell, which
# is the claim 2b makes and the one that would be silently wrong if the oracle
# treated a mutable cell as a hole -- every segment built from these would be
# rejected and nobody would find out why. A fixture with a safe way round could
# not tell the difference.

name = test_mutable
base_height = 0
width = 5
length = 8
tags = foot, test, mutable

